      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Limit at Positive or Negative Infinity Using L'Hopital's Rule",
      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+16}=$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying  L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+16} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{[{x}^{2}-1]^{′}}{[x+16]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{2x}{1} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
